@startuml dispatch_runtime_flow
title Dispatch runtime — terminal release (direct), retry (through allocation), tick dispatch (autonomous daemon)\nNo drain trigger anywhere; the three paths are decoupled.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1
skinparam linetype polyline

actor "Fleet (Modal/Vast/Community)" as FLEET
participant "JobsRouter\n(api/routers)"          as ROUTER
participant "JobService"                          as JOBSVC
participant "Lifecycle"                           as LC
participant "ModalActiveJobsHooks"                as MHOOKS
participant "InProgressChunkRepository\n(shared, repositories/)" as INPROG
participant "AllocationClient\n(orchestrator)"   as CLIENT
participant "AllocationFacade\n(allocation)"     as FACADE
participant "AllocationPlanningService"           as PLAN
participant "AllocationDispatchQueueService"      as DQS
participant "AllocationDispatchQueueRepository"   as QREPO
participant "AllocationDispatchQueueDaemon\n(allocation, background)" as DAEMON
participant "AllocationDispatcher"                as DISP
participant "FleetStrategy"                       as STRAT

== PATH A — fleet job ends (callback → release; no allocation involvement) ==
FLEET   -> ROUTER  : POST /jobs/{id}/status (succeeded|failed)
ROUTER  -> JOBSVC  : update_status
JOBSVC  -> LC      : handle_chunk_succeeded(job) | handle_chunk_failed(job)

LC      -> INPROG  : release(group_id, chunk_index)

alt fleet == "modal_serverless"
    LC -> MHOOKS : on_terminal(job_id, gpu_type)
end

note over LC, INPROG
  No allocation calls.
  Lifecycle clears the dedup ledger directly via the shared repo
  (the same repo allocation also writes to during dispatch).
  Freed cap headroom will be picked up by the next daemon tick.
end note

== PATH B — retry decision (failure → plan + enqueue, through allocation) ==
note over LC
  When handle_chunk_failed decides retry-yes,
  RetryPipelineRunner runs the steps below.
end note
LC      -> CLIENT  : plan_retry_for_chunk(req, tier, snapshot)
CLIENT  -> FACADE  : plan_retry(strategy_name, req, snapshot)
FACADE  -> PLAN    : plan_retry(strategy_name, req, snapshot)
PLAN   --> FACADE  : PlannedTask | None
FACADE --> CLIENT  : PlannedTask | None
LC      -> CLIENT  : enqueue(group_id, [task], ctx)
CLIENT  -> FACADE  : enqueue(group_id, [task], ctx)
FACADE  -> DQS     : enqueue(group_id, [task], ctx)
DQS     -> QREPO   : enqueue(group_id, item)
note over LC, QREPO
  Pure write. No dispatch happens here.
  Daemon picks it up on next tick.
end note

== PATH C — daemon tick (the only place dispatch fires) ==
loop every tick (~2s, gated by Redis singleton lock)
    DAEMON -> DQS : dispatch_pending_for_fleet(fleet)
    loop while cap headroom AND queue non-empty
        DQS -> DQS    : active_count_by_fleet()  (Callable -> JobRepository)
        DQS -> QREPO  : dequeue_for_fleet(fleet)
        QREPO --> DQS : AllocationQueueItem | None
        DQS -> INPROG : claim_or_replace(group_id, chunk_index, job_id, attempt)
        DQS -> DISP   : dispatch_one(task, ctx, job_id)
        DISP -> STRAT : dispatch(task, ctx, job_id)
        STRAT --> DISP : DispatchResult
    end
end

note over DAEMON, STRAT
  Only one Cloud Run replica's daemon ticks at a time
  (Redis lock, same pattern as MonitorLockSweeper).
  Daemon never calls Lifecycle, never knows about retries,
  never knows about callbacks. It only empties the queue
  within fleet caps, claiming the dedup ledger as it goes.
end note

@enduml
